  "description": "Bug lane, LITE (report with a ## Repro block -> intake -> envelope -> RCA -> envelope -> ONE human gate -> envelope -> RED test -> fix loop -> negcontrol -> review -> negcontrol -> draft PR). For small, locally reproducible bugs only: setup/lite-envelope.sh refuses tickets outside setup/lite-envelope.json with ROUTE=FULL before the RCA, before the gate, and again after approval; relaunch the same report on bugfix. No prod evidence, no chain verification, no smoke matrix: the proof is the repro test going RED -> GREEN plus two negative controls. Run message = ABSOLUTE path to the bug report. Owns ports 4126/3126. Invoke with DISABLE_OMC=1. GENERATED by setup/derive-lite.py from bugfix.yaml + setup/lite/bugfix.json + setup/lite/bugfix/ - never hand-edit.",
